  "question": {
    "text": "The correct statements about the oxoacids, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HClO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>and</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>HClO</mi></math>&nbsp;are,",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "5rsIJ",
      "text": "the conjugate base of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HClO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> is weaker base than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HClO</mi></math>.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "uTWMi",
      "text": "the central atom in both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HClO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HClO</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math>is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> hybridized.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "GGC5K",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HClO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> is formed in the reaction between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>and</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0my84",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HClO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> is more acidic than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HClO</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math>because of the resonance stabilization of its anion.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(i)  <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HClO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mo>⇌</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>ClO</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi></mrow></msubsup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>ClO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math>  is resonance stabilized anion.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HClO</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mo>⇌</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ClO</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo>  </mo><mo>  </mo><msub><mi>HClO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> is more acidic then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HClO</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>(ii)   <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>HClO</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>HCl</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi></math></p><p>(iii)  <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HClO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/25_solu_chem_pa1.jpg\"/>The central atom is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> hybridised.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/25_solu_chem_pa1_2.jpg\"/> The central atom is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> hybridised.</p><p>(iv)  <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HClO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>→</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>⊕</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>ClO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math> since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> is accepting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math> from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HClO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> so <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>  is stronger base compare to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>ClO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math>.</p>",
